    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Section 15",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Section 21 of the Principal Act is amended—\n(a) by omitting paragraph (a) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\" (a) a person who is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship—\n(i) has been convicted of an offence against section 50 in\nrelation to the application for his certificate of\nAustralian citizenship; or\n(ii) has, at any time after furnishing the application for his\ncertificate of Australian citizenship (including a time\nafter the grant of the certificate), been convicted of an\noffence against a law in force in a foreign country or\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or Territory\nfor which he has been sentenced to death or to\nimprisonment for life or for a period of not less than 12\nmonths, being an offence committed at any time before\nthe grant of the certificate (including a time before the\nfurnishing of the application); and\";\n(b) by inserting \"in his discretion,\" after \"the Minister may,\"; and\n(c) by adding at the end thereof the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) A reference in sub-section (1) to a conviction of an offence\nincludes a reference to the making of an order under sub-section\n19B (1) of the Crimes Act 1914 ox the corresponding provision of a\nlaw in force in a foreign country or of a law of a State or Territory in\nrelation to the offence.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where the Minister makes an order under sub-section (1)\ndepriving a person of his Australian citizenship, the Minister shall, if\nthe person is present in Australia, cause to be served on the person,\neither personally or by post, a copy of that order.\".\nChildren of persons who lose or are deprived of citizenship",
      "skos:definition": "Section 21 of the Principal Act is amended—\n(a) by omitting paragraph (a) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\" (a) a person who is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship—\n(i) has been convicted of an offence against section 50 in\nrelation to the application for his certificate of\nAustralian citizenship; or\n(ii) has, at any time after furnishing the application for his\ncertificate of Australian citizenship (including a time\nafter the grant of the certificate), been convicted of an\noffence against a law in force in a foreign country or\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or Territory\nfor which he has been sentenced to death or to\nimprisonment for life or for a period of not less than 12\nmonths, being an offence committed at any time before\nthe grant of the certificate (including a time before the\nfurnishing of the application); and\";\n(b) by inserting \"in his discretion,\" after \"the Minister may,\"; and\n(c) by adding at the end thereof the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) A reference in sub-section (1) to a conviction of an offence\nincludes a reference to the making of an order under sub-section\n19B (1) of the Crimes Act 1914 ox the corresponding provision of a\nlaw in force in a foreign country or of a law of a State or Territory in\nrelation to the offence.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where the Minister makes an order under sub-section (1)\ndepriving a person of his Australian citizenship, the Minister shall, if\nthe person is present in Australia, cause to be served on the person,\neither personally or by post, a copy of that order.\".\nChildren of persons who lose or are deprived of citizenship",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-15-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-15-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-15-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "880221e3ea984eda8b15911b885b9ce79374b6b8c41dfe6b15d2b094f5776c3d",
      "skos:note": "A person who is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of Australian citizenship cannot have been convicted of certain offences."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Section 15",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Section 21 of the Principal Act is amended—\n(a) by omitting paragraph (a) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\" (a) a person who is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship—\n(i) has been convicted of an offence against section 50 in\nrelation to the application for his certificate of\nAustralian citizenship; or\n(ii) has, at any time after furnishing the application for his\ncertificate of Australian citizenship (including a time\nafter the grant of the certificate), been convicted of an\noffence against a law in force in a foreign country or\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth, a State or Territory\nfor which he has been sentenced to death or to\nimprisonment for life or for a period of not less than 12\nmonths, being an offence committed at any time before\nthe grant of the certificate (including a time before the\nfurnishing of the application); and\";\n(b) by inserting \"in his discretion,\" after \"the Minister may,\"; and\n(c) by adding at the end thereof the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) A reference in sub-section (1) to a conviction of an offence\nincludes a reference to the making of an order under sub-section\n19B (1) of the Crimes Act 1914 ox the corresponding provision of a\nlaw in force in a foreign country or of a law of a State or Territory in\nrelation to the offence.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where the Minister makes an order under sub-section (1)\ndepriving a person of his Australian citizenship, the Minister shall, if\nthe person is present in Australia, cause to be served on the person,\neither personally or by post, a copy of that order.\".\nChildren of persons who lose or are deprived of citizenship"
    },
