    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-16-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes a duty on the State to ensure responsible parents maintain their children's citizenship.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Minister shall cause to be served on the person, either personally or by post, a copy of that order.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The State must provide notice to the person before directing them to cease being an Australian citizen."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-16-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the temporal interval during which the Minister's order takes effect.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) if the cessation referred to in paragraph (c) is by reason of the\ndeath of the responsible parent—at any time after that death.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The order takes effect at least 30 days after the responsible parent's death."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-16-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Grants permission to the Minister to direct children to cease being Australian citizens.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) Where, but for this sub-section—\n(a) a child would cease to be an Australian citizen under\nsub-section (1) as a consequence of a responsible parent of the\nchild ceasing to be an Australian citizen;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister may direct children to cease being Australian citizens."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 After section 23 of the Principal Act the following section is inserted:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 17 in certain\ncircumstances\n\" 2 3 A A . (1) Where a person does an act or thing that, under section 17,\nresults in the person ceasing to be an Australian citizen and—\n(a) if he did not do the act or thing, he would have suffered significant\nhardship or detriment; or\n(b) at the time he did the act or thing he did not know that he would, as a\nconsequence of his doing the act or thing, cease to be an Australian\ncitizen,\nthe person may make and furnish to the Minister a statement to that effect and\na declaration in accordance with the prescribed form that he wishes to resume\nAustralian citizenship.\n\"(2) The Minister may, in his discretion, if he is satisfied as to the truth of\nthe statement made by a person for the purposes of sub-section (1), and, in a\ncase where the person has claimed that, if he had not done the act or thing that\nresulted in his ceasing to be an Australian citizen, he would have suffered\nhardship or detriment of an economic nature, that the person's circumstances\nwere such as to compel him to do that act or thing, register the declaration in\nthe prescribed manner and, upon the registration of the declaration, the person\nmaking the declaration again becomes an Australian citizen.\".\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 20",
      "skos:definition": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 17 in certain\ncircumstances\n\" 2 3 A A . (1) Where a person does an act or thing that, under section 17,\nresults in the person ceasing to be an Australian citizen and—\n(a) if he did not do the act or thing, he would have suffered significant\nhardship or detriment; or\n(b) at the time he did the act or thing he did not know that he would, as a\nconsequence of his doing the act or thing, cease to be an Australian\ncitizen,\nthe person may make and furnish to the Minister a statement to that effect and\na declaration in accordance with the prescribed form that he wishes to resume\nAustralian citizenship.\n\"(2) The Minister may, in his discretion, if he is satisfied as to the truth of\nthe statement made by a person for the purposes of sub-section (1), and, in a\ncase where the person has claimed that, if he had not done the act or thing that\nresulted in his ceasing to be an Australian citizen, he would have suffered\nhardship or detriment of an economic nature, that the person's circumstances\nwere such as to compel him to do that act or thing, register the declaration in\nthe prescribed manner and, upon the registration of the declaration, the person\nmaking the declaration again becomes an Australian citizen.\".\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 20",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-17-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-17-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-17-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3ffb1e52fc7c0318bbc05c144aa3e9cc7d052e5de6ffc55cfab42a07f6d1923e",
      "skos:note": "A person may make a statement and declaration to resume citizenship lost under section 17.",
      "dc:description": "Statement and Declaration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 After section 23 of the Principal Act the following section is inserted:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 17 in certain\ncircumstances\n\" 2 3 A A . (1) Where a person does an act or thing that, under section 17,\nresults in the person ceasing to be an Australian citizen and—\n(a) if he did not do the act or thing, he would have suffered significant\nhardship or detriment; or\n(b) at the time he did the act or thing he did not know that he would, as a\nconsequence of his doing the act or thing, cease to be an Australian\ncitizen,\nthe person may make and furnish to the Minister a statement to that effect and\na declaration in accordance with the prescribed form that he wishes to resume\nAustralian citizenship.\n\"(2) The Minister may, in his discretion, if he is satisfied as to the truth of\nthe statement made by a person for the purposes of sub-section (1), and, in a\ncase where the person has claimed that, if he had not done the act or thing that\nresulted in his ceasing to be an Australian citizen, he would have suffered\nhardship or detriment of an economic nature, that the person's circumstances\nwere such as to compel him to do that act or thing, register the declaration in\nthe prescribed manner and, upon the registration of the declaration, the person\nmaking the declaration again becomes an Australian citizen.\".\nPersons may resume citizenship lost under section 20"
    },
