    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Section 20",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "Section 23D of the Principal Act is amended by omitting sub-sections\n(2) and (3) and substituting the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) Where the Minister makes a decision under sub-section (1) refusing\nan application and the applicant is present in Australia, the Minister shall cause\nto be served on the applicant, either personally or by post, a notice in writing\nsetting out that decision.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment No. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where—\n(a) but for this sub-section, section 10B would prevent the acquisition of\nAustralian citizenship by a person by reason only of all or any of the\nfollowing matters:\n(i) that more than 18 years have elapsed since the birth of the\nperson;\n(ii)\nthat\nthe requirement\nset out in\nsub-sub-paragraph\n10B (1) (b) (ii) (B) is not fulfilled by either of the persons who\nwere the parents of the first-mentioned person at the time of his\nbirth;\n(iii) the operation of sub-section 10B (2); and\n(b) the first-mentioned person is not, and has never been, a citizen of any\ncountry,\nthen—\n(c) the name of the first-mentioned person may be registered for the\npurposes of section 10B; and\n(d) the matter or matters referred to in paragraph (a) does not or do not\nprevent the acquisition of Australian citizenship by the person under\nsection 10B.\n\" ( 3 A ) Where, but for this sub-section, a person to whom sub-paragraph\n21 (1) (a) (ii) applies would, if the Minister were to make an order under\nsub-section 21 (1) in relation to that person, become a person who is not a\ncitizen of any country, sub-section 21 (1) does not apply in relation to that\nperson.\".\nTransitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "Section 23D of the Principal Act is amended by omitting sub-sections\n(2) and (3) and substituting the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) Where the Minister makes a decision under sub-section (1) refusing\nan application and the applicant is present in Australia, the Minister shall cause\nto be served on the applicant, either personally or by post, a notice in writing\nsetting out that decision.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment No. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where—\n(a) but for this sub-section, section 10B would prevent the acquisition of\nAustralian citizenship by a person by reason only of all or any of the\nfollowing matters:\n(i) that more than 18 years have elapsed since the birth of the\nperson;\n(ii)\nthat\nthe requirement\nset out in\nsub-sub-paragraph\n10B (1) (b) (ii) (B) is not fulfilled by either of the persons who\nwere the parents of the first-mentioned person at the time of his\nbirth;\n(iii) the operation of sub-section 10B (2); and\n(b) the first-mentioned person is not, and has never been, a citizen of any\ncountry,\nthen—\n(c) the name of the first-mentioned person may be registered for the\npurposes of section 10B; and\n(d) the matter or matters referred to in paragraph (a) does not or do not\nprevent the acquisition of Australian citizenship by the person under\nsection 10B.\n\" ( 3 A ) Where, but for this sub-section, a person to whom sub-paragraph\n21 (1) (a) (ii) applies would, if the Minister were to make an order under\nsub-section 21 (1) in relation to that person, become a person who is not a\ncitizen of any country, sub-section 21 (1) does not apply in relation to that\nperson.\".\nTransitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-20-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-20-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "54e0e890ce2a5e9ab80d939e3441d43733bd27d22565777e5e87e024dc1548fd",
      "skos:note": "Minister must serve notice on applicant if decision is refused and applicant is present in Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Section 20",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "Section 23D of the Principal Act is amended by omitting sub-sections\n(2) and (3) and substituting the following sub-sections:\n\"(2) Where the Minister makes a decision under sub-section (1) refusing\nan application and the applicant is present in Australia, the Minister shall cause\nto be served on the applicant, either personally or by post, a notice in writing\nsetting out that decision.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment No. 129, 1984\n\"(3) Where—\n(a) but for this sub-section, section 10B would prevent the acquisition of\nAustralian citizenship by a person by reason only of all or any of the\nfollowing matters:\n(i) that more than 18 years have elapsed since the birth of the\nperson;\n(ii)\nthat\nthe requirement\nset out in\nsub-sub-paragraph\n10B (1) (b) (ii) (B) is not fulfilled by either of the persons who\nwere the parents of the first-mentioned person at the time of his\nbirth;\n(iii) the operation of sub-section 10B (2); and\n(b) the first-mentioned person is not, and has never been, a citizen of any\ncountry,\nthen—\n(c) the name of the first-mentioned person may be registered for the\npurposes of section 10B; and\n(d) the matter or matters referred to in paragraph (a) does not or do not\nprevent the acquisition of Australian citizenship by the person under\nsection 10B.\n\" ( 3 A ) Where, but for this sub-section, a person to whom sub-paragraph\n21 (1) (a) (ii) applies would, if the Minister were to make an order under\nsub-section 21 (1) in relation to that person, become a person who is not a\ncitizen of any country, sub-section 21 (1) does not apply in relation to that\nperson.\".\nTransitional provisions"
    },
