      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Sections 34 and 35 of the Principal Act are repealed and the following\nsection is substituted:\nPosthumous children\n\"34. (1) A reference in this Act to the status or description of a parent of a\nperson at the time of the person's birth shall, in the case of a parent who died\nbefore the birth of the person, be read as a reference to the status or description\nof the parent at the time of the parent's death.\n\"(2) Where the death of a parent of a person occurred prior to, and the\nbirth of the person occurred after, the commencement of this section, the status\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nor description that would have been applicable to the parent by virtue of\nsub-section (1) if the parent had died after the commencement of the section\nshall be deemed to be the status or description applicable to the parent at the\ntime of the death of the parent.\".\nStatement in support of application for certificate of Australian citizenship",
      "skos:definition": "Sections 34 and 35 of the Principal Act are repealed and the following\nsection is substituted:\nPosthumous children\n\"34. (1) A reference in this Act to the status or description of a parent of a\nperson at the time of the person's birth shall, in the case of a parent who died\nbefore the birth of the person, be read as a reference to the status or description\nof the parent at the time of the parent's death.\n\"(2) Where the death of a parent of a person occurred prior to, and the\nbirth of the person occurred after, the commencement of this section, the status\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nor description that would have been applicable to the parent by virtue of\nsub-section (1) if the parent had died after the commencement of the section\nshall be deemed to be the status or description applicable to the parent at the\ntime of the death of the parent.\".\nStatement in support of application for certificate of Australian citizenship",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-24-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2df861d20e6d8e5923f055289ebdf30f3921ef740183a982c767b2a0cb24e7c8",
      "skos:note": "Repeals sections 34 and 35 of the Principal Act, substituting a new section regarding posthumous children."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Section 24",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Sections 34 and 35 of the Principal Act are repealed and the following\nsection is substituted:\nPosthumous children\n\"34. (1) A reference in this Act to the status or description of a parent of a\nperson at the time of the person's birth shall, in the case of a parent who died\nbefore the birth of the person, be read as a reference to the status or description\nof the parent at the time of the parent's death.\n\"(2) Where the death of a parent of a person occurred prior to, and the\nbirth of the person occurred after, the commencement of this section, the status\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nor description that would have been applicable to the parent by virtue of\nsub-section (1) if the parent had died after the commencement of the section\nshall be deemed to be the status or description applicable to the parent at the\ntime of the death of the parent.\".\nStatement in support of application for certificate of Australian citizenship"
    },
