    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Section 31",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "Sections 48, 48A and 49 of the Principal Act are repealed and the\nfollowing sections are substituted:\nReplacement certificates\n\"47A. Where the Minister proposes to amend a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'original certificate') under section\n47, not being an amendment including the name of a person in, or omitting the\nname of a person from, the original certificate, the Minister may, in his\ndiscretion, in lieu of so amending the original certificate, upon surrender of the\noriginal certificate to him, grant and issue a further certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'replacement certificate') in which\nthat amendment has been incorporated and thereupon the replacement\ncertificate has effect for all purposes of this Act as if it had been granted and\nissued at the same time as the original certificate and the original certificate had\nnot been granted.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nSurrender of certificates\n\"48. (1) Where an order is made under this Act depriving a person of his\nAustralian citizenship—\n(a) if that person is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship granted to him—that person shall, upon\ndemand in writing by the Minister, surrender that certificate to the\nMinister for cancellation; and\n(b) if that person is an Australian citizen by reason of the inclusion of his\nname in a certificate of Australian citizenship granted to another\nperson—that other person shall, upon demand in writing by the\nMinister, surrender that certificate to the Minister to enable the\nMinister to amend that certificate under section 47.\n\"(2) Where an order is made under sub-section 44A (4) revoking an\nevidentiary certificate issued to a person under section 44A, the person shall,\nupon demand in writing by the Secretary, surrender the certificate to the\nSecretary for cancellation.\n\"(3) A person who, without reasonable excuse, contravenes sub-section\n(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not\nexceeding $1,000.\nOffence to alter certificate\n\"49. A person shall not, without lawful authority, alter, or cause or permit\nto be altered, a certificate of Australian citizenship.\nPenalty: $2,000 or imprisonment for 12 months, or both.\".\nFalse representations, &c.",
      "skos:definition": "Sections 48, 48A and 49 of the Principal Act are repealed and the\nfollowing sections are substituted:\nReplacement certificates\n\"47A. Where the Minister proposes to amend a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'original certificate') under section\n47, not being an amendment including the name of a person in, or omitting the\nname of a person from, the original certificate, the Minister may, in his\ndiscretion, in lieu of so amending the original certificate, upon surrender of the\noriginal certificate to him, grant and issue a further certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'replacement certificate') in which\nthat amendment has been incorporated and thereupon the replacement\ncertificate has effect for all purposes of this Act as if it had been granted and\nissued at the same time as the original certificate and the original certificate had\nnot been granted.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nSurrender of certificates\n\"48. (1) Where an order is made under this Act depriving a person of his\nAustralian citizenship—\n(a) if that person is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship granted to him—that person shall, upon\ndemand in writing by the Minister, surrender that certificate to the\nMinister for cancellation; and\n(b) if that person is an Australian citizen by reason of the inclusion of his\nname in a certificate of Australian citizenship granted to another\nperson—that other person shall, upon demand in writing by the\nMinister, surrender that certificate to the Minister to enable the\nMinister to amend that certificate under section 47.\n\"(2) Where an order is made under sub-section 44A (4) revoking an\nevidentiary certificate issued to a person under section 44A, the person shall,\nupon demand in writing by the Secretary, surrender the certificate to the\nSecretary for cancellation.\n\"(3) A person who, without reasonable excuse, contravenes sub-section\n(1) or (2) i",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-31-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-31-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0efa58f0062f3fb6633e62ae202f3ac5c18e4565d8765a8f8248965125be45dd",
      "skos:note": "Substitutes new sections for repealed ones, with conditions on certificate surrender."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Section 31",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "Sections 48, 48A and 49 of the Principal Act are repealed and the\nfollowing sections are substituted:\nReplacement certificates\n\"47A. Where the Minister proposes to amend a certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'original certificate') under section\n47, not being an amendment including the name of a person in, or omitting the\nname of a person from, the original certificate, the Minister may, in his\ndiscretion, in lieu of so amending the original certificate, upon surrender of the\noriginal certificate to him, grant and issue a further certificate of Australian\ncitizenship (in this section referred to as the 'replacement certificate') in which\nthat amendment has been incorporated and thereupon the replacement\ncertificate has effect for all purposes of this Act as if it had been granted and\nissued at the same time as the original certificate and the original certificate had\nnot been granted.\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nSurrender of certificates\n\"48. (1) Where an order is made under this Act depriving a person of his\nAustralian citizenship—\n(a) if that person is an Australian citizen by virtue of a certificate of\nAustralian citizenship granted to him—that person shall, upon\ndemand in writing by the Minister, surrender that certificate to the\nMinister for cancellation; and\n(b) if that person is an Australian citizen by reason of the inclusion of his\nname in a certificate of Australian citizenship granted to another\nperson—that other person shall, upon demand in writing by the\nMinister, surrender that certificate to the Minister to enable the\nMinister to amend that certificate under section 47.\n\"(2) Where an order is made under sub-section 44A (4) revoking an\nevidentiary certificate issued to a person under section 44A, the person shall,\nupon demand in writing by the Secretary, surrender the certificate to the\nSecretary for cancellation.\n\"(3) A person who, without reasonable excuse, contravenes sub-section\n(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not\nexceeding $1,000.\nOffence to alter certificate\n\"49. A person shall not, without lawful authority, alter, or cause or permit\nto be altered, a certificate of Australian citizenship.\nPenalty: $2,000 or imprisonment for 12 months, or both.\".\nFalse representations, &c."
    },
