    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-35",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35 After section 52 of the Principal Act the following sections are inserted:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-35"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nReview of decisions\n\" 5 2 A . (1) Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of—\n(a) decisions of the Minister under section 13 or sub-section 23D ( 1 )\nrefusing an application;\n(b) decisions of the Minister under section 18 other than decisions under\nsub-section 18 (5);\n(c) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 21 (1) or 23 (2) or section\n47;\n(d) decisions of the Minister, the Secretary, or a person authorized by the\nSecretary for the purposes of section 23A or 23B, under that section;\nand\n(e) decisions of the Minister under sub-section\n23AA (2) refusing to\nregister a declaration.\n\"(2) A person is not entitled to make an application under sub-section (1)\nfor review of a decision under section 13 (other than sub-section 13 (9)) unless\nthe person is a permanent resident.\n\"(3) In this section, 'decision' has the same meaning as in the\nAdministrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975.\nStatement to accompany notification of decisions\n\" 5 2 B . (1) Where the Minister or a delegate of a Minister makes a decision\nof the kind referred to in section 52A and gives, or causes to be given, to a\nperson or persons whose interests are affected by the decision notice in writing\nof the decision, that notice shall include a statement to the effect that, subject to\nthe Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 and to sub-section 52A (2) of\nthis Act, application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of the decision to which the notice relates by or on behalf of a person or\npersons whose interests are affected by the decision.\n\"(2) Any failure to comply with the requirements of sub-section (1) in\nrelation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision.\".\nRegulations",
      "skos:definition": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nReview of decisions\n\" 5 2 A . (1) Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of—\n(a) decisions of the Minister under section 13 or sub-section 23D ( 1 )\nrefusing an application;\n(b) decisions of the Minister under section 18 other than decisions under\nsub-section 18 (5);\n(c) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 21 (1) or 23 (2) or section\n47;\n(d) decisions of the Minister, the Secretary, or a person authorized by the\nSecretary for the purposes of section 23A or 23B, under that section;\nand\n(e) decisions of the Minister under sub-section\n23AA (2) refusing to\nregister a declaration.\n\"(2) A person is not entitled to make an application under sub-section (1)\nfor review of a decision under section 13 (other than sub-section 13 (9)) unless\nthe person is a permanent resident.\n\"(3) In this section, 'decision' has the same meaning as in the\nAdministrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975.\nStatement to accompany notification of decisions\n\" 5 2 B . (1) Where the Minister or a delegate of a Minister makes a decision\nof the kind referred to in section 52A and gives, or causes to be given, to a\nperson or persons whose interests are affected by the decision notice in writing\nof the decision, that notice shall include a statement to the effect that, subject to\nthe Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 and to sub-section 52A (2) of\nthis Act, application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of the decision to which the notice relates by or on behalf of a person or\npersons whose interests are affected by the decision.\n\"(2) Any failure to comply with the requirements of sub-section (1) in\nrelation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision.\".\nRegulations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-35-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-35-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8c7fe15b5cae22430d164948bc70f012b06d4a9858ea5498dc836ec9d4fb7f2a",
      "skos:note": "Applications for review of certain decisions can be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984#sec-35",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35 After section 52 of the Principal Act the following sections are inserted:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "Australian Citizenship Amendment\nNo. 129, 1984\nReview of decisions\n\" 5 2 A . (1) Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal for review of—\n(a) decisions of the Minister under section 13 or sub-section 23D ( 1 )\nrefusing an application;\n(b) decisions of the Minister under section 18 other than decisions under\nsub-section 18 (5);\n(c) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 21 (1) or 23 (2) or section\n47;\n(d) decisions of the Minister, the Secretary, or a person authorized by the\nSecretary for the purposes of section 23A or 23B, under that section;\nand\n(e) decisions of the Minister under sub-section\n23AA (2) refusing to\nregister a declaration.\n\"(2) A person is not entitled to make an application under sub-section (1)\nfor review of a decision under section 13 (other than sub-section 13 (9)) unless\nthe person is a permanent resident.\n\"(3) In this section, 'decision' has the same meaning as in the\nAdministrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975.\nStatement to accompany notification of decisions\n\" 5 2 B . (1) Where the Minister or a delegate of a Minister makes a decision\nof the kind referred to in section 52A and gives, or causes to be given, to a\nperson or persons whose interests are affected by the decision notice in writing\nof the decision, that notice shall include a statement to the effect that, subject to\nthe Administrative\nAppeals Tribunal Act 1975 and to sub-section 52A (2) of\nthis Act, application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for\nreview of the decision to which the notice relates by or on behalf of a person or\npersons whose interests are affected by the decision.\n\"(2) Any failure to comply with the requirements of sub-section (1) in\nrelation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision.\".\nRegulations"
    },
